X:728
T:Keel Rewe Reel. JBut.724, The
T:Keel Row. JBut.724, The
T:Smiling Polly, aka. JBut.724
N:A setting of the well known tune, "The Keel Row".
N:The R in  "Rewe" could, possibly, be read as a B, but Rewe is a contemporary spelling of "Row"
N:Thought to be of Scottish, or Northumbrian in origin.
N:aka Smiling Polly, Thompson's Compleat Collection of 200 Favourite Country Dances, vol. 2, 1765, No. 129. (VMP THO2.129
N:Very similar A Part (in D). B Part, less so.
N:The tune is in the Northumbrian music manuscript collection of John Smith, dated 1752, unfortunately now lost
N:(information from The Traditional Tune Archive).
B:John Buttrey MS, poss. Lincolnshire, early 19thC
S:https://buttreymilitarysocialtunes1800.wordpress.com/
