X:732
T:Wounded Hussay. JBut.728, The
N:This tune was originally scored in 6/8, a usual time signature of  The Wounded Hussar. However, is has been
N:heavily over written by modifications converting it to common time.
N:The A Part appears to have had 5 bars and the B Part However, it is
N:not unique in this respect.Other settings of this tune have unusual numbers of bars.
N:The tune is transcribed, so far as possible, as it might have been intended, however
N:it is, sometimes,  difficult to make sense of the intention because the overwriting is very heavy.
B:John Buttrey MS, poss. Lincolnshire, early 19thC
S:https://buttreymilitarysocialtunes1800.wordpress.com/
Z:vmp.2019.Greg Bradfield-Smith.
